(5935126, 863130, 100301, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EL-ROI:</b></div><hr/><i> A very respectable top ten finish on this! I like your work with the XSi. Do you process your raw in DPP and then go to photoshop? Also to speak to one of the comments regarding sharpness, did you adjust the sharpness in camera settings or just use the default setting of 3 and sharpen afterwards? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Honestly there was no sharpness processing.  I didn''t shoot this in RAW either, I just adjusted the curves, levels, vibrance and saturation.  I think the sharpness critique is coming from the natural texture of the rock maybe?  But the commenter didn''t make it clear if his sharpness concerns were too sharp or not enough.   anyhow, here is the original... <br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=865841" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100301/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_865841.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100301/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_865841.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/100000-104999/100301/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_865841.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Originally posted by EL-ROI: A very respectable top ten finish on this! I like your work with the XSi. Do you process your raw in DPP and then go to photoshop? Also to speak to one of the comments regarding sharpness, did you adjust the sharpness in camera settings or just use the default setting of 3 and sharpen afterwards?   Honestly there was no sharpness processing.  I didn''t shoot this in RAW either, I just adjusted the curves, levels, vibrance and saturation.  I think the sharpness critique is coming from the natural texture of the rock maybe?  But the commenter didn''t make it clear if his sharpness concerns were too sharp or not enough.   anyhow, here is the original...  ', '2010-04-07 10:43:18.000000', NULL, 0),
